1. Loan Terms

1.1 Loan Amount
The Lender shall make a loan in the principal amount of $[5,000,000] to the Borrower.

1.2 Loan Term
The term of this loan shall be $[5] years, commencing on the date of this agreement and ending on the date five (5) years from such date (the "Maturity Date").

1.3 Maturity Date
The principal amount of the loan and any accrued but unpaid interest shall be due and payable in full on the Maturity Date.

1.4 Amortization Schedule
The Borrower shall make regular principal and interest payments as set forth in the amortization schedule attached hereto as Exhibit A.

1.5 Interest Rate
The interest rate for the loan shall be the base rate of $[X]% per annum, plus $[Y]% per annum, as adjusted from time to time in accordance with the terms of this agreement.

1.6 Payment Schedule
The Borrower shall make payments in accordance with the payment schedule set forth in the amortization schedule attached hereto as Exhibit A.

1.7 Loan Disbursements
The Lender shall disburse the loan proceeds to the Borrower in one or more installments as agreed between the parties.

1.8 Use of Proceeds
The Borrower shall use the proceeds of the loan solely for the purpose of financing its [research and development] activities.

1.9 Loan Documentation
The Borrower shall execute and deliver to the Lender such additional documentation as the Lender may reasonably require in connection with this loan.

1.10 Prepayment
The Borrower shall have the right to prepay all or any part of the loan, without penalty, at any time prior to the Maturity Date.

1.11 Extension
The Lender and the Borrower may agree in writing to extend the Maturity Date of the loan.

1.12 Transfer of Loan
The Borrower shall not assign, transfer, pledge, hypothecate, or otherwise encumber this loan without the prior written consent of the Lender.

1.13 Loan Modification
The Lender and the Borrower may agree in writing to modify the terms of this loan.

2. Interest and Fees

2. Interest and Fees

2.1 Interest Rate
The interest rate for the loan shall be the base rate of $[X]% per annum, plus $[Y]% per annum, as adjusted from time to time in accordance with the terms of this agreement.

2.2 Interest-Only Payments
For the first [Z] months following the Disbursement Date, the Borrower shall make only interest payments, with the principal payments commencing on the [A]th month following the Disbursement Date.

2.3 Fees
The Borrower shall pay the following fees in connection with this loan:

(a) Commitment Fee: A commitment fee of $[W]% of the loan amount shall be paid to the Lender on the Disbursement Date.

(b) Origination Fee: An origination fee of $[V]% of the loan amount shall be paid to the Lender on the Disbursement Date.

(c) Documentation Fee: A documentation fee of $[U] shall be paid to the Lender upon execution of this agreement.

(d) Late Fee: A late fee of $[T]% of the unpaid principal and interest shall be charged to the Borrower for each day that any payment is overdue, up to a maximum of $[S]%.

(e) Legal Fee: The Borrower shall reimburse the Lender for all reasonable legal fees and expenses incurred in connection with this loan.

2.4 Payment Schedule
The Borrower shall make payments in accordance with the payment schedule set forth in the amortization schedule attached hereto as Exhibit A.

3. Security

3. Security

3.1 Collateral
The collateral securing this loan shall consist of the following assets owned by the Borrower:

(a) Accounts Receivable: All accounts receivable of the Borrower, including all amounts due and owing from customers of the Borrower as of the Disbursement Date, and all amounts due and owing from customers of the Borrower that are generated during the term of this loan.

(b) Inventory: All inventory of the Borrower, including raw materials, work in progress, and finished goods, as of the Disbursement Date, and all inventory that is generated during the term of this loan.

(c) Equipment: All equipment owned by the Borrower as of the Disbursement Date, and all equipment that is acquired during the term of this loan.

(d) Intellectual Property: All intellectual property owned by the Borrower as of the Disbursement Date, and all intellectual property that is developed during the term of this loan.

(e) Real Property: All real property owned by the Borrower as of the Disbursement Date, and all real property that is acquired during the term of this loan.

3.2 Security Agreement
The Borrower shall execute a security agreement in favor of the Lender, securing the loan with the collateral described in this Section 3.1.

3.3 Right to Offset
The Lender shall have the right to set off any amounts owed by the Borrower to the Lender against any amounts owed by the Lender to the Borrower.

3.4 Right to Sell Collateral
In the event of default by the Borrower, the Lender shall have the right to sell the collateral securing the loan, in its sole discretion, to satisfy the outstanding loan balance and any accrued interest, fees, and expenses.

3.5 Proceeds of Sale
The Borrower shall be entitled to any proceeds of the sale of the collateral in excess of the outstanding loan balance, accrued interest, fees, and expenses.

3.6 Appraisal
The Borrower shall arrange for an appraisal of the collateral securing the loan at the time of the Disbursement Date and at such other times as the Lender may reasonably request.

3.7 Insurance
The Borrower shall maintain insurance on the collateral securing the loan, with the Lender as the beneficiary, in an amount and with terms satisfactory to the Lender.

3.8 Change of Collateral
The Borrower shall promptly notify the Lender of any change in the collateral securing the loan, and the parties shall agree in writing on any necessary modifications to this agreement.

4. Representations and Warranties

4. Representations and Warranties

4.1 Lender's Representations and Warranties
The Lender hereby represents and warrants to the Borrower as follows:

4.1.1 Authority
The Lender has the legal power and authority to enter into this agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

4.1.2 Loan Documents
The Loan Documents have been duly executed and delivered by the Lender and constitute legal, valid, and binding obligations of the Lender, enforceable against the Lender in accordance with their terms, except as may be limited by applicable bankruptcy, insolvency, reorganization, moratorium, or other laws of general applicability affecting the enforcement of creditors' rights and remedies.

4.1.3 Collateral
The Lender has taken all necessary action to perfect its security interest in the collateral, and such security interest is valid, perfected, and enforceable against third parties.

4.2 Borrower's Representations and Warranties
The Borrower hereby represents and warrants to the Lender as follows:

4.2.1 Authority
The Borrower has the legal power and authority to enter into this agreement and to perform its obligations hereunder.

4.2.2 Loan Purpose
The proceeds of the loan will be used solely for the purpose of financing the [research and development] activities of the Borrower.

4.2.3 Financial Statements
The financial statements provided to the Lender in connection with this loan are true and complete in all material respects.

4.2.4 Guarantor
The Guarantor has the legal power and authority to enter into the Guaranty and to perform its obligations thereunder.

4.2.5 No Default
As of the Disbursement Date, there is no default under any material agreement to which the Borrower is a party or by which it is bound.

4.2.6 No Liens
As of the Disbursement Date, there are no liens, encumbrances, or other security interests on the collateral securing the loan, except for those created by this agreement.

4.2.7 Compliance with Laws
The Borrower is in compliance with all applicable laws, regulations, and governmental orders relating to its business, operations, and the collateral securing the loan.

4.2.8 No Conflicts
The execution, delivery, and performance of this agreement by the Borrower do not conflict with, or constitute a default under, any agreement to which the Borrower is a party or by which it is bound.

5. Covenants

5. Covenants

5.1 Borrower's Obligations
The Borrower covenants and agrees as follows:

5.1.1 Repayment
The Borrower will make the payments as set forth in Section 2, on the dates specified therein, in the amounts specified therein, and in the manner specified therein.

5.1.2 Financial Ratios
The Borrower will maintain the financial ratios set forth in Exhibit A, as such ratios may be amended from time to time by the Lender in its sole discretion.

5.1.3 Financial Statements
The Borrower will provide the Lender with the financial statements set forth in Exhibit B on the dates specified therein.

5.1.4 Notices
The Borrower will promptly provide the Lender with written notice of any material changes in its business, operations, or financial condition that could reasonably be expected to materially affect the Borrower's ability to repay the loan.

5.2 Lender's Obligations
The Lender covenants and agrees as follows:

5.2.1 No Unilateral Changes
The Lender will not make any unilateral changes to the terms of the loan, except as expressly provided in this agreement.

5.2.2 No Waiver
The failure of the Lender to insist upon strict performance by the Borrower of any of the Borrower's obligations under this agreement will not operate as a waiver of such obligation or of any subsequent breach thereof.

5.2.3 Access to Books and Records
The Lender will have the right to inspect and copy the books and records of the Borrower, including financial statements, tax returns, and other relevant documents, during regular business hours upon reasonable notice.

5.2.4 No Conflicts
The Lender will not engage in any activity that conflicts with, or impairs the Lender's ability to perform its obligations under this agreement.

5.3 Guarantor's Obligations
The Guarantor covenants and agrees as follows:

5.3.1 No Waiver
The failure of the Guarantor to insist upon strict performance by the Borrower of any of the Borrower's obligations under this agreement will not operate as a waiver of such obligation or of any subsequent breach thereof.

5.3.2 Access to Books and Records
The Guarantor will have the right to inspect and copy the books and records of the Borrower, including financial statements, tax returns, and other relevant documents, during regular business hours upon reasonable notice.

5.3.3 No Conflicts
The Guarantor will not engage in any activity that conflicts with, or impairs the Guarantor's ability to perform its obligations under the Guaranty.

6. Default and Remedies

6. Default and Remedies

6.1 Events of Default
The following events shall constitute events of default under this agreement:

6.1.1 Failure to Pay
The Borrower's failure to pay any principal or interest on the Loan when due, or the Borrower's failure to pay any fees or expenses as required by this agreement.

6.1.2 Breach of Covenants
The Borrower's breach of any of its covenants, representations, or warranties contained in this agreement.

6.1.3 Insolvency
The Borrower's filing of a petition in bankruptcy, or the appointment of a receiver or trustee for the Borrower or for all or substantially all of the Borrower's assets.

6.1.4 Default by Guarantor
The default by the Guarantor under the Guaranty.

6.2 Remedies
Upon the occurrence of an event of default, the Lender shall have the following remedies, without limitation:

6.2.1 Acceleration
The Lender may declare all amounts owing under this agreement immediately due and payable.

6.2.2 Security Interest
The Lender may exercise its rights and remedies with respect to the collateral, including taking possession thereof and selling the same, subject to applicable law.

6.2.3 Judicial Remedies
The Lender may bring suit against the Borrower and the Guarantor for the collection of any amounts due under this agreement, and may obtain injunctive relief or specific performance to enforce the terms of this agreement.

6.2.4 Other Remedies
The Lender may pursue any other remedies available at law or in equity.

6.3 Notice
The Lender may give notice of an event of default to the Borrower and the Guarantor by written notice, delivered in person, by registered or certified mail, or by facsimile or email. The notice shall specify the nature of the default and the remedies available to the Lender under this agreement.

6.4 Cure
The Borrower and the Guarantor shall have 30 days from the date of receipt of the notice of default to cure the default. If the default is not cured within the 30-day period, the Lender may exercise its remedies as provided in this agreement.

6.5 Waiver
The failure of the Lender to insist upon strict performance by the Borrower or the Guarantor of any of their obligations under this agreement, or any prior agreement, will not operate as a waiver of such obligation or of any subsequent breach thereof.

6.6 Successors and Assigns
The rights and remedies of the Lender under this agreement shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the Lender's successors and assigns. The Borrower and the Guarantor may not assign their rights or delegate their obligations under this agreement without the prior written consent of the Lender.

